            <title><![CDATA[Study reveals energy demands and emissions of America's data centers]]></title>
            <link>https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/study-reveals-energy-demands-and-emissions-of-americas-data-centers</link>
            <description><![CDATA[The 400 largest data centers in the United States emit more greenhouse gas emissions in one year than the entire nation of Denmark, according to a new report from Harvard University. From May 2024 to April 2025, data centers accounted for nearly 2% of total U.S. energy consumption and produced more than 25 million metric tons of CO2. Amna Nawaz spoke with the study's lead author, Gianluca Guidi.]]></description>
